    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0253" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7–2547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-25T10:00:00+09:00">July 25, 1947—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 28—5:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>178. Cheng Tung-kuo, Acting Commander NECC, informed Colonel Barrett,<anchor
                        n="36" xml:id="d198-f1"/> A[ssistant] Military Attaché, July 25: <pb
                        facs="0254" n="244" xml:id="pg244"/><list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Nationals in Manchuria unable effect counteroffensive without
                            reinforcements provided existing acute shortage ammunition and equipment
                            relieved.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>No independent Korean units operating with Communists NE. Considerable
                            numbers Korean with Communist armies but are integrated into regular
                            Chinese units.</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>Only few very old pieces equipment captured from Communists by
                            Nationals. Does not believe Russia supplying Communists Soviet equipment
                            which latter would give away Soviet policy to United States. Are
                            supplying Communists Jap equipment only.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
